  "title": "Radix checkpoint reanchors ownership and prefill reserves future capacity separately",
  "mechanism": "RadixCache.checkpoint excludes an already-evicted SWA prefix, inserts the eligible key, rematches it and rewrites the request row to the tree-owned indices. The protected length is only the cached aligned prefix; a partial page remains request-owned. It releases the old lock and locks the new last node. Lock-reference transitions move token counts between evictable and protected categories only at zero-to-one and one-to-zero boundaries. PrefillBudget admits its total-token check only when requested total is strictly less than remaining total, while immediate paged allocation uses a less-than-or-equal comparison against both current and total capacity. reserve page-aligns the extension, adds an extra page and optional extra tokens to both offsets, and charges max_new_tokens only to total_offset. These inequalities and headroom charges serve distinct admission decisions.",
  "corrections": [
    "Do not treat partial-page tokens outside cache_protected_len as tree-owned.",
    "Do not replace the two admission inequalities with one generic available-capacity rule.",
    "The selected subset does not verify page-interleaved communication or backend integration."
  ],
  "source_scope": "Manually read the listed exact Git ranges for the final corrected mechanism. All other model claims remain research notes; no runtime experiment.",
